// DOES THIS REPO SHIP TO THE STORE? The whole release half of this pack is gated on
// it, coded rule and declared checks alike — coding an extension pulls the pack in
// (its fingerprint is the manifest), and a repo that never publishes must not be
// asked for a release config, a privacy page or a README release section.
//
// The signal is the ORCHESTRATOR'S NAME, not a path: Claudinite's own core tree
// carries a file at the same path named "… (reusable)", so a path test would make the
// canon fingerprint itself. The legacy name still counts — a repo whose orchestrator
// predates the rename is shipping, and cer/release-workflows is what tells it to
// rename (#1057; it was this pack's `detect` before the collapse).
//
// DUPLICATED, DELIBERATELY: the declared checks in declared-checks.json cannot import,
// so each carries the same test as a `relevantWhen.someTrackedFileContains` regex.
// packs-tests/chrome-extension/pack.test.mjs runs both over one matrix of repos and
// fails if they ever disagree — keep this literal unbroken so that guard, and any
// grep, still sees it.
